# /etc/wgft/server.env - dotenv read by default by the server (VPS-side daemon) and the CLI.
# Install with mode 0644: the provided server.service runs as an unprivileged user and must be able
# to read it. No setting here is secret; keys, certificates and tokens live in the database.
#
# Format: one KEY=value per line. Only a leading # starts a comment. Do not quote values or
# include spaces in them. (This is the subset that Docker --env-file, compose env_file and the
# binary itself all read the same way.)
#
# Settings (flag alias in parentheses). Required: WGFT_WG_ENDPOINT, and WGFT_MODE on the first start.
# Everything else has a default.
#   WGFT_MODE            Forwarding mode, kernel or userspace (--mode). Required on the first start,
#                        which records it in the database. On later starts, if omitted, the recorded
#                        mode is used; if set, it is checked against the recorded one
#   WGFT_WG_ENDPOINT     REQUIRED. host:port that the agents connect to (--wg-endpoint): a domain or IP
#                        of this VPS plus the WireGuard UDP port, for example vps.example.com:51820
#   WGFT_WG_INTERFACE    WireGuard interface name (--wg-interface, default wgft0)
#   WGFT_WG_PORT         WireGuard listen UDP port (--wg-port, default 51820)
#   WGFT_WG_ADDRESS      WireGuard address range (--wg-address, default 10.200.0.1/24). Recorded on the
#                        first start and checked against on every later start
#   WGFT_AGENT_API       agent API listen address (--agent-api, default 0.0.0.0:8443, public)
#   WGFT_AGENT_API_HOST  host:port written into join strings (--agent-api-host, default: the host of
#                        WGFT_WG_ENDPOINT plus the port of WGFT_AGENT_API)
#   WGFT_ADMIN           admin API listen address (--admin, default unix:///run/wgft/admin.sock)
#   WGFT_ADMIN_TAILSCALE also listen on the tailnet address (--admin-tailscale, true/false). Detected
#                        first from `tailscale status --json`; falls back to an interface named
#                        tailscale0, or tailscale*, when the tailscale CLI is missing or fails. The
#                        MagicDNS name from `tailscale status` is added to the allowed Host names too
#   WGFT_ADMIN_HOST      extra Host names accepted by the admin API, comma separated (--admin-host)
#   WGFT_MTU             WireGuard MTU (--mtu, default 1420; lower it on a thin link)
#   WGFT_DATA_DIR        data directory (--data-dir, default /var/lib/wgft; holds wgft.sqlite)
#   WGFT_MAX_UDP_FLOWS   process-wide cap on concurrent UDP sessions (--max-udp-flows, default 8192)
#   WGFT_MAX_TCP_FLOWS   process-wide cap on concurrent TCP connections (--max-tcp-flows, default 2048).
#                        In the lab, 2048 UDP / 1024 TCP ran inside a 150 MiB cgroup in userspace mode;
#                        this has not yet been verified on a real 256 MiB VPS
#   WGFT_MAX_UDP_FLOWS_PER_SOURCE  cap on concurrent UDP sessions from one source address, summed
#                        over all rules (--max-udp-flows-per-source, default 256). 0 disables it.
#                        Server-only: the agent cannot tell source addresses apart (its peer is
#                        always the server), so it has no such setting
#   WGFT_MAX_TCP_FLOWS_PER_SOURCE  same, for TCP connections (--max-tcp-flows-per-source, default 128)
#
# Note: if the VPS already runs a WireGuard whose listen port equals WGFT_WG_PORT, the server
# refuses to start (exit code 3). Pick a free port and make the port in WGFT_WG_ENDPOINT match
# (for example 51821 when the existing one uses 51820).
# Run `sudo wgft server check` before starting to inspect the config and the environment
# (existing WireGuard, ports, other nftables tables).

WGFT_MODE=kernel
WGFT_WG_ENDPOINT=vps.example.com:51820
